        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="true" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="3">
                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="1" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="0" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>During the inspection we notice air leakage from the following house components:

- WINDOWS:

     Basement: (x2) The big window in the basement living room (FRONT) and the windows on the rear side of the house

     Main: (x2) The small office and the guest room

     2nd: (x4) Windows in living room and in the kitchen

-DOORS:

     Tha garage door in the basement

     The outside door on the left side (access to patio over garage)



The leakage are not so bad, maybe only the replacement of the weather strips will be good enough to seal the units and the doors.

                              </airSeal>
                <ceilings>We estimate the level of insulation of the roof to be R-40 (12'') we recommend the addition of insulation to reach a level of R-60 or even R-70.</ceilings>
                <windows>During the infiltration test we notice some air leaks around the windows frame. Must of the windows looses heat and therefore increase the heat loss inside the house. We recommend the replacement of the windows by ENERGY STAR certified units.</windows>
                <doors>We notice some air leakage from the doors. The air leakage have been observed on the garage door located in the basement and the deck door on the top floor. We recommend the replacement of the doors seals. If the problem is not resolved you might have to replace the unit. If replacement of the door we recommend the ENERGY STAR certified doors.</doors>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
